-- Same unit (M) on both sides but mismatched numpy dtype (float32 vs float64).
-- Distinct from testBadAssignmentNDArrayElement (which uses a plain "float", not even
-- a numpy dtype): this specifically exercises method_fullname resolving __setitem__ on a
-- CompoundType receiver, and the numpy_sipy plugin correctly reconstructing
-- CompoundType(unit, scalar_type) per overload so the mismatch is still caught when the
-- unit matches and only the wrapped numeric dtype differs.
[case testBadAssignmentNDArrayElementUnitDtypeMismatch]
